            </note>
            <note corresp="#d505-f2" n="3" xml:id="d505-f2-content">
                <p>Vyacheslav Mikhailovich Molotov, Soviet Minister of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d505-f3" n="4" xml:id="d505-f3-content">
                <p>Georges Bidault, French Minister for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d505-f4" n="5" xml:id="d505-f4-content">
                <p>Ernest Bevin, British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d505-f5" n="6" xml:id="d505-f5-content">
                <p>Section IV of the communiqué” on the Moscow Conference of the Three Foreign
                    Ministers, December 27, 1945; Department of State <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bulletin</hi>, December 30, 1945, p. 1030, or <ref
                        target="frus1945v02#pg_815">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1945, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp. 815</ref>, <ref
                        target="frus1945v02#pg_821">821</ref>.</p>
            </note>
